  "details": "As of build 737 I am experiencing an issue with onnetworkready triggers of masterunbuffered type on my map. This was not present in build 735. \n\nMap: Bedroom Theatre\nID: wrld_fff5d510-fc53-4e88-9d4e-1e0e45a17aff\n\nEdit:\n--\ni've updated the public map to mitigate the issue using a different trigger type, for reproduction please use\nMap: Bedroom Theatre - Build 737 issue\nID: wrld_a47e2f62-131c-47c8-93f7-a76847574e5f\n--\n\nReproduction steps: Just load into the map. By design master is detected, a noticable audio queue is played, and given control over the video controls, but now they are not.\n\nThere is an error, attached in the screenshot \"[VRC_EventLog] Could not find instigator for [SendRPC/MasterUnbuffered w: -1 s: Play i: 6 f: 0 b: False B: 8 p: /RoomAccessControl/MasterAccess/MasterLocal]\"\n\nI am not able to confirm if broadcast types other than masterunbuffered are affected, if someone else could that'd be great.",
